{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Core-Middleware","text":"Core Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs keypaths to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" properties."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" needs "},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so it can snapshot and compare."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","text":"Domain Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites","text":"Importing at call sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"separate library target","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"core Swidux only","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"that","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches "},{"code":"store.analytics.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"AnalyticsAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"touches only "},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":".ui(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The easy case to forget is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" that reads the slice for display — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The fix is to add ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Swidux<Plugin>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Comparison","level":3,"text":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Core Middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain Plugins","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lifecycle hooks"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns effects"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State coupling"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" constraint","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wiring"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construction only","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"text":" library","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Separate library target","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2,"text":"The Decision Rule"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2,"text":"Hook Selection Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2,"text":"Registration Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2,"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"text":"Next Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","roleHeading":"Article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","title":"Undo \/ Redo","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","abstract":[{"text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observation layer.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Store","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Security Posture","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"PluginHost","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"role":"article","title":"Design Principles","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"}}}